# Xero MCP (Phase 0)

Secure, hands-off OAuth + Cursor wiring for the official [`@xeroapi/xero-mcp-server`](https://github.com/XeroAPI/xero-mcp-server).

**Location:** `tools/xero-mcp/`

## Design goals

| Goal | How |
|------|-----|
| **Secure** | Client secret in macOS Keychain; tokens in `~/.config/xero-mcp/` (mode 600); pinned npm version; audit log never stores tokens |
| **Hands-off** | Refresh token rotated automatically; launchd agent refreshes every 15 min; MCP wrapper refreshes on each Cursor start |
| **Auditable in Xero** | Fixed app name in Connected apps; transaction history in Xero; local `doctor` + `audit.log` for auth events |

## One-time setup (~5 min)

Create a **Web app** at [developer.xero.com](https://developer.xero.com/app/manage/):

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| App name | `Cursor MCP (Mac)` (must match — visible in Xero Connected apps) |
| Type | Web app |
| Redirect URI | `http://localhost:8765/callback` (not `127.0.0.1` — Xero rejects it) |

Then run:

```bash
export XERO_CLIENT_ID="..."
export XERO_CLIENT_SECRET="..."
bash /Users/topexnative/Projects/unraid-array-design/tools/xero-mcp/scripts/setup-phase0.sh
```

This will: store secret in Keychain → OAuth once → install token keeper → wire Cursor → print health check.

Reload Cursor MCP servers once. After that, **no routine hands-on** is required.

## Day-to-day (zero touch)

- **Cursor** starts Xero MCP → token refreshed automatically
- **launchd** runs `xero_mcp maintain` every 15 minutes
- Refresh tokens are long-lived; browser login is only needed again if you revoke the app in Xero

## Check anytime

```bash
cd /Users/topexnative/Projects/unraid-array-design/tools/xero-mcp
source .venv/bin/activate
python -m xero_mcp doctor
```

**In the Xero app (each organisation):**

1. Open the org → **Settings** → **General Settings** → **Connected apps**
2. Find **`Cursor MCP (Mac)`** — confirms API access is active
3. Click **Disconnect** to revoke instantly (MCP stops working until you `login` again)

**Transaction audit:** Invoices, bills, contacts, and payments created via MCP appear in normal Xero history (invoice History & Notes, etc.).

**Developer portal:** [developer.xero.com/app/manage/](https://developer.xero.com/app/manage/) shows your app and connection stats.

## CLI reference

| Command | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `python -m xero_mcp init` | Save client id; secret → Keychain |
| `python -m xero_mcp login` | One-time browser OAuth |
| `python -m xero_mcp doctor` | Health + where to verify in Xero |
| `python -m xero_mcp maintain` | Token refresh + `health.json` (used by launchd) |
| `python -m xero_mcp status` | JSON auth state |
| `python -m xero_mcp token` | Valid access token (internal; never log) |

## Security model

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  macOS Keychain          ~/.config/xero-mcp/ (700/600)  │
│  ─ client_secret         ─ connections.json (tokens)    │
│                          ─ credentials.json (no secret) │
│                          ─ health.json (status)         │
│                          ─ audit.log (auth events only) │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                              │
                    Cursor MCP wrapper (localhost only)
                              │
                         Xero API (TLS)
```

- **Never committed:** secrets, tokens, audit log
- **OAuth:** PKCE + `offline_access` for refresh tokens
- **Revocation:** Disconnect in Xero Connected apps — takes effect immediately
- **Supply chain:** `@xeroapi/xero-mcp-server@0.0.17` pinned in wrapper (override with `XERO_MCP_SERVER_VERSION`)

## Re-auth (rare)

Only needed if you revoked the app or refresh token expired:

```bash
python -m xero_mcp login
python -m xero_mcp doctor
```

## Files

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `~/.config/xero-mcp/credentials.json` | App name, client id, scopes (no secret) |
| macOS Keychain `xero-mcp-client-secret` | Client secret |
| `~/.config/xero-mcp/connections.json` | OAuth tokens + org list |
| `~/.config/xero-mcp/health.json` | Last automated health check |
| `~/.config/xero-mcp/audit.log` | Auth/refresh events (JSON lines, no tokens) |
| `~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.unraid-array-design.xero-mcp-token-keeper.plist` | 15-min refresh agent |

## Multi-org (Phase 1)

Two MCP servers work together:

| Server | Role |
|--------|------|
| **xero-orgs** | `list_organisations`, `set_active_organisation`, `get_active_organisation` |
| **xero** | Official accounting tools (invoices, contacts, items, …) |

**Agent workflow:** call `set_active_organisation` on **xero-orgs** with a slug or company name, then use **xero** tools. Switch is instant — no MCP restart.

```bash
python -m xero_mcp list-orgs
python -m xero_mcp use-org matariki-traders
```

Org slugs (auto-generated from Xero names):

| Slug | Company |
|------|---------|
| `matariki-property-group` | Matariki Property Group Limited |
| `matariki-traders` | Matariki Traders Limited |
| `matariki-morningside-development` | Matariki Morningside Development Limited |

Default org: set `default_slug` in `/Users/topexnative/.config/xero-mcp/orgs.config.json` (copy from `xero.orgs.example.json`).

Install Phase 1:

```bash
bash /Users/topexnative/Projects/unraid-array-design/tools/xero-mcp/scripts/setup-phase1.sh
```

The official server is patched locally (`patches/xero-client.js`) to read `~/.config/xero-mcp/active-org.json` on every API call.

## Troubleshooting

| Issue | Fix |
|-------|-----|
| **403 Forbidden** on login | Redirect URI must be `http://localhost:8765/callback` in **both** Xero developer portal and local config — Xero blocks `127.0.0.1` |
| `doctor` shows re-auth | `python -m xero_mcp login` |
| MCP won't start | `python -m xero_mcp doctor` — check `last_error` |
| Revoked in Xero | Expected — reconnect with `login` |
| Token keeper not loaded | `bash scripts/install-token-keeper.sh` |
| Wrong org selected | `python -m xero_mcp use-org matariki-traders` or **xero-orgs** `set_active_organisation` |
